{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread","id":1382398,"title":"The Chicago Folio discussion thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-18T15:29:58-07:00","id":1382398,"title":"The Chicago Folio discussion thread","content":"Well, I have my hardcopy of the Chicago Folios and did up my review of it: <a href=\"http://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/1786-thechicagofolios\" target=\"_blank\">http://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/1...echicagofolios</a><br /> <br /> What did you guys think of it?<br /> <br /> I have to say I didn't think I would get much out of this book because I just thought it would be a bunch of adventure hooks. However, I think this book did give a lot of extra flavor for the Chicago region post CBN5E and while some of the adventures aren't great (&quot;Balthazar wants you to key the Prince's car!&quot;), I felt a lot of them were solid enough to provide a night's adventuring. I think there's also some really good NPCs in the book as well. My favorite being Joseph Peterson's childe and her lesbian Russian fighter pilot lover. That's just the kind of weird off-brand Kindred relationship that works well.<br /> <br /> Some other thoughts:<br /> <br /> * <b>Al Capone's Survival</b>: A lot of V:TM fans have never been fond of Al Capone for the very same reason that he's hunted by Kevin Jackson: He's just too high profile a figure to be a vampire. It's like Elvis being undead. However, I think the version done up here is a very solid one and him as a puppetmaster from behind the scenes works well.<br /> <br /> * <b>The Sabbat</b>: We're all desperate for any information on the Sabbat so the Seven Fires are just a tiny write-up about them but gives at least a little bit of an idea of what they're up to. It confirms that at least some of the sect is still operating and gives us some terrifying stories too. I also liked how <b>Samson</b>, the dumbest Sabbat ever, is made to be legitimately terrifying.<br /> <br /> * <b>The Second Inquisition</b>: I like how they're depicted as conducting horrifying experiments as part of their modus apparandi. They really give the Second Inquisition a nasty undercurrent of psychopathia and callousness that adds to their WoD flavor.<br /> <br /> * <b>Shejana</b>: While the fact the Ravnos are now considered Caitiff will bother some, I like that she's been given a write-up as she was my favorite new character of Chicago by Night 2nd Edition. I also like how her illusion powers are enough to screw with all of Chicago.<br /> <br /> * <b>Blackjack</b>: Joshua Tarponski being the Baron of a small city outside of Chicago where he's lord of like 5-6 Kindred works for me, personally. I think it's a nice little retirement for a fun character that I was worried had met the Final Death. I'm also interested in his relationship to the Church of Caine.<br /> <br /> Art is gorgeous as always too. A big improvement over the main books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T15:51:39-07:00","id":1382401,"title":"","content":"I'm a big fan of the Loresheets introduced in the folio, especially Kindred Dueling and Malkavian Family. Kindred hobbies and the setting-level oddities of Malkavians are two of my favorite things to hear about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T18:12:21-07:00","id":1382417,"title":"","content":"Is there any thing in this for folks that don't want to set games in Chicago?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T18:15:39-07:00","id":1382418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1382417#post1382417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any thing in this for folks that don't want to set games in Chicago?</div> </div> </div> </div>The lore sheets do apply outside of it, like Kindred Dueling or many of the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T01:34:03-07:00","id":1382468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1382417#post1382417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any thing in this for folks that don't want to set games in Chicago?</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost all of the adventure hooks are pretty generic street level ones. They may use Chicago NPCs but can be adapted very easily, IMHO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T12:18:44-07:00","id":1382569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1382417#post1382417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any thing in this for folks that don't want to set games in Chicago?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b><i>Pretty much everything in the book can be adapted to any city of your choosing</i></b>.<br /> <br /> The rituals can be learned easily enough, by meeting the right person at the right time.<br /> <br /> Loresheets are always a welcome inclusion into any of my games, some may need to be reworded to fit your campaign, but not hard to do.<br /> <br /> As CTPhipps mentioned: the story hooks are generic enough that they can be used anywhere.<br /> <br /> NPCs(spcs) Can easily be transposed into new areas, or change their Names/Clans/Disciplines to create your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26038-feargrounds","name":"FearGrounds","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T18:27:43-07:00","id":1382653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread#post1382398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I have my hardcopy of the Chicago Folios and did up my review of it: <a href=\"http://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/1786-thechicagofolios\" target=\"_blank\">http://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/1...echicagofolios</a><br /> <br /> What did you guys think of it?<br /> <br /> I have to say I didn't think I would get much out of this book because I just thought it would be a bunch of adventure hooks. However, I think this book did give a lot of extra flavor for the Chicago region post CBN5E and while some of the adventures aren't great (&quot;Balthazar wants you to key the Prince's car!&quot;), I felt a lot of them were solid enough to provide a night's adventuring. I think there's also some really good NPCs in the book as well. My favorite being Joseph Peterson's childe and her lesbian Russian fighter pilot lover. That's just the kind of weird off-brand Kindred relationship that works well.<br /> <br /> Some other thoughts:<br /> <br /> * <b>Al Capone's Survival</b>: A lot of V:TM fans have never been fond of Al Capone for the very same reason that he's hunted by Kevin Jackson: He's just too high profile a figure to be a vampire. It's like Elvis being undead. However, I think the version done up here is a very solid one and him as a puppetmaster from behind the scenes works well.<br /> <br /> * <b>The Sabbat</b>: We're all desperate for any information on the Sabbat so the Seven Fires are just a tiny write-up about them but gives at least a little bit of an idea of what they're up to. It confirms that at least some of the sect is still operating and gives us some terrifying stories too. I also liked how <b>Samson</b>, the dumbest Sabbat ever, is made to be legitimately terrifying.<br /> <br /> * <b>The Second Inquisition</b>: I like how they're depicted as conducting horrifying experiments as part of their modus apparandi. They really give the Second Inquisition a nasty undercurrent of psychopathia and callousness that adds to their WoD flavor.<br /> <br /> * <b>Shejana</b>: While the fact the Ravnos are now considered Caitiff will bother some, I like that she's been given a write-up as she was my favorite new character of Chicago by Night 2nd Edition. I also like how her illusion powers are enough to screw with all of Chicago.<br /> <br /> * <b>Blackjack</b>: Joshua Tarponski being the Baron of a small city outside of Chicago where he's lord of like 5-6 Kindred works for me, personally. I think it's a nice little retirement for a fun character that I was worried had met the Final Death. I'm also interested in his relationship to the Church of Caine.<br /> <br /> Art is gorgeous as always too. A big improvement over the main books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brilliant addition to Chicago by Night; really expands the info from that book and really happy to discover info on Al Capone at last!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/337-joe","name":"Joe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T09:59:50-07:00","id":1383972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread#post1382398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* <b>Shejana</b>: While the fact the Ravnos are now considered Caitiff will bother some, I like that she's been given a write-up as she was my favorite new character of Chicago by Night 2nd Edition. I also like how her illusion powers are enough to screw with all of Chicago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does she have Chimerstry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T10:05:58-07:00","id":1383973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Riccardo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1383972#post1383972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does she have Chimerstry?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, just Dominate and Presence but she's described as having combinations that allow her to do illusions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T12:05:05-07:00","id":1383988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Riccardo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1383972#post1383972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does she have Chimerstry?</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the V5 design philosophy, as far as Disciplines are concerned, is that no clan should have their own, unique Discipline. Hence why Thaumaturgy and Quietus have been folded together into Blood Sorcery (makes sense to me, since the Haqimites always had their own brand of blood sorcery), Serpentis is folded into Protean, etc. I know some people still chafe at this design choice, but I honestly don't mind it, since I was never a huge fan of some clans have unique Disciplines and other, well, not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T15:09:37-07:00","id":1384040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1383988#post1383988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part of the V5 design philosophy, as far as Disciplines are concerned, is that no clan should have their own, unique Discipline. Hence why Thaumaturgy and Quietus have been folded together into Blood Sorcery (makes sense to me, since the Haqimites always had their own brand of blood sorcery), Serpentis is folded into Protean, etc. I know some people still chafe at this design choice, but I honestly don't mind it, since I was never a huge fan of some clans have unique Disciplines and other, well, not.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like they're planning to use Dominate as part of the Chimerstry amalgam, and I think that's dumb because Obfuscate + Fortitude seems like a perfect amalgam for making long-lasting illusions. Obfuscate was already about changing the senses, and then you can say that Fortitude makes those changes more tangible.<br /> <br /> I personally am a fan of removing &quot;unique&quot; Disciplines and putting together all those which are thematically similar, but I think some of them were implemented poorly. Like the Eyes of the Serpent power that reflects Serpentis, which was folded into Protean...why is Eyes of the Serpent then a PRESENCE power with a Protean amalgam, rather than a Protean power with a Presence amalgam?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T15:15:23-07:00","id":1384041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1384040#post1384040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems like they're planning to use Dominate as part of the Chimerstry amalgam, and I think that's dumb because Obfuscate + Fortitude seems like a perfect amalgam for making long-lasting illusions. Obfuscate was already about changing the senses, and then you can say that Fortitude makes those changes more tangible.<br /> <br /> I personally am a fan of removing &quot;unique&quot; Disciplines and putting together all those which are thematically similar, but I think some of them were implemented poorly. Like the Eyes of the Serpent power that reflects Serpentis, which was folded into Protean...why is Eyes of the Serpent then a PRESENCE power with a Protean amalgam, rather than a Protean power with a Presence amalgam?</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be argued that dominate or presence can affect the senses so using them with obfuscate makes a good way to represent the illusion effect of the power. Making stuff tangible out of thin air always was an high level application of chimerstry anyway. Is making a real sword appear out of thin air more important to the discipline than making people believe something happened when it did not? Fortitude only makes sense in combination with Chimerstry to mimic a very specific subsect of the discipline powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T09:52:08-07:00","id":1384208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1383973#post1383973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope, just Dominate and Presence but she's described as having combinations that allow her to do illusions.</div> </div> </div> </div>What a great new! Ventrues can cast illusion now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T11:10:20-07:00","id":1384224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1384208#post1384208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What a great new! Ventrues can cast illusion now.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the big appeals of v5 for me is the fact you're now allowed to have way different power sets.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T11:44:26-07:00","id":1384233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1384224#post1384224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the big appeals of v5 for me is the fact you're now allowed to have way different power sets.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Ventrue could have always gained access to Chimerstry if they made the effort to. In V5 a lot of the amalgams are made to be readily accessible to one clan, and others could learn them if they put in the effort to imitate that clan. Only a Malkavian has the innate disciplines to pick up the Dominate/Obfuscate blend of Dementation, but a Ventrue or Tremere who practiced hiding or a Nosferatu who practiced mind control could also learn it pretty easily. But if Chimerstry is somehow Dominate/Presence then it's just as innately Ventrue as it would be Ravnos, and that seems weird. No Ventrue would have to go to any effort to learn it.<br /> That's why I suggested Obfuscate/Fortitude as an amalgam, it would be hard for anyone (except I guess Samedi?) to have that combo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T14:13:17-07:00","id":1384262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1384233#post1384233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Ventrue could have always gained access to Chimerstry if they made the effort to. In V5 a lot of the amalgams are made to be readily accessible to one clan, and others could learn them if they put in the effort to imitate that clan. Only a Malkavian has the innate disciplines to pick up the Dominate/Obfuscate blend of Dementation, but a Ventrue or Tremere who practiced hiding or a Nosferatu who practiced mind control could also learn it pretty easily. But if Chimerstry is somehow Dominate/Presence then it's just as innately Ventrue as it would be Ravnos, and that seems weird. No Ventrue would have to go to any effort to learn it.<br /> That's why I suggested Obfuscate/Fortitude as an amalgam, it would be hard for anyone (except I guess Samedi?) to have that combo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but they were all the same power sets.<br /> <br /> Now with Protean you can become an owl or a panther. Powers vary tremendously now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T14:33:32-07:00","id":1384269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1384262#post1384262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but they were all the same power sets.<br /> <br /> Now with Protean you can become an owl or a panther. Powers vary tremendously now.</div> </div> </div> </div>On contrary. In REVISED you could became owl or panther. <br /> In v5 you can raw only turn into thematic animals. <br /> But ventrues with chimerstry is a v5 exclusive bright invention for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T15:13:49-07:00","id":1384277,"title":"","content":"No CTPhilps is correct, you can change into an Owl or Panther via basic protean powers. Large Feline is even an example.<br /> <br /> And as said previously Illusions will probably be an obfuscate amalgam with dominate or presence so unless the Ventrue have Obfuscate in-clan, they will not have access any faster than they would needed to learn Chimerstry before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","user":"Redwulfe","date":". 04-27-2020, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T04:50:00-07:00","id":1384392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1384277#post1384277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No CTPhilps is correct, you can change into an Owl or Panther via basic protean powers. Large Feline is even an example.<br /> <br /> And as said previously Illusions will probably be an obfuscate amalgam with dominate or presence so unless the Ventrue have Obfuscate in-clan, they will not have access any faster than they would needed to learn Chimerstry before.</div> </div> </div> </div>He said presence and dominate amalgam.<br /> Anyway, I am glad Ventrues or Malkavians or &quot;Ministry of Love&quot; remain without chimerstry as a in clan discipline power in v20. <br /> <br /> About the protean power, in revised gangrel clanbook say the player choose 1 fight 1 flee form that can be many things, like a shark etc.<br /> <br /> In v5, it is said NEED to be thematic apropriate at the same time say the vampire can turn into lion or whatever. Cant remember the last book/movie/mythos about vampires turning in lions but you do you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T08:40:57-07:00","id":1384413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1384392#post1384392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He said presence and dominate amalgam.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1383973#post1383973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope, just Dominate and Presence but she's described as having combinations that allow her to do illusions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though this is not what I was referring to, he did not say that it was a dominate and Presence amalgam it is two statements separated by a &quot;but&quot; that you seem to have combined in your assumption. She can create illusions is separate from her having Dominate and Presence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1384040#post1384040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems like they're planning to use Dominate as part of the Chimerstry amalgam, and I think that's dumb because Obfuscate + Fortitude seems like a perfect amalgam for making long-lasting illusions. Obfuscate was already about changing the senses, and then you can say that Fortitude makes those changes more tangible.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I was pointing to when I said it was pointed out that it was a part of the Amalagm not the whole. This spoke of Obfuscate as a part. It has been discussed a lot in the V5 communities. What will combine with Obfuscate in the Chimerstry amalgam. Some say Dominate some say Presence. My point was though it seems you are trying to make fun of things, that comes from your misunderstanding and not where they ridiculously give Ventrue Illusions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1384392#post1384392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the protean power, in revised gangrel clanbook say the player choose 1 fight 1 flee form that can be many things, like a shark etc.<br /> <br /> In v5, it is said NEED to be thematic apropriate at the same time say the vampire can turn into lion or whatever. Cant remember the last book/movie/mythos about vampires turning in lions but you do you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not talking about previous editions only V5. Page 270 and 271 Shapechange and Metamorphosis powers. it does not say it NEEDS to be thematic at all. All it just says that you USUALLY change into a form associated with your clan, because others such as the ministry and old clan will have protean if not more OR it will be based on the type of pray you most commonly feed on. so if you are a Gangrel in south america or Africa a large cat would be fine or if you just want to choose that as a shape it OK. That is why it says usually it is up to you.<br /> <br /> The misconception that I am trying to point out is that these rules are somehow rigid and unmovable. they are not. You have the choice so its not &quot;me doing me&quot; it is you'all can do whatever you wish. the players and STs of the game have agency to play the way they want to. Just like every edition of the game ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","user":"Redwulfe","date":". 04-28-2020, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T08:42:53-07:00","id":1384415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1384392#post1384392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In v5, it is said NEED to be thematic apropriate at the same time say the vampire can turn into lion or whatever. Cant remember the last book/movie/mythos about vampires turning in lions but you do you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is to prevent people from turning into vampire rabbits or other ridiculous critters, Thematic means that it fits a vampire.<br /> <br /> And yes, I can easily see lion vampires, preferrably if the vampire is from an area with them.<br /> <br /> THE GHOST IN THE DARKNESS for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T11:03:29-07:00","id":1384447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1384392#post1384392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In v5, it is said NEED to be thematic apropriate at the same time say the vampire can turn into lion or whatever. Cant remember the last book/movie/mythos about vampires turning in lions but you do you.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's absolutely no written requirement that the animal be &quot;thematically appropriate.&quot; All the book says is &quot;The vampire can assume the shape of an animal roughly the same size as their original mass. The vampire can only change into one type of animal (usually a wolf, sometimes a large feline or a giant snake), usually one associated with their clan or the type of prey they most commonly feed on.&quot; So it has to be roughly human-sized/weighted, and it's usually associated with either clan or feeding. You could justify turning into any kind of animal if you make a point to feed on that type, and more importantly the use of the word &quot;usually&quot; means that they don't HAVE to have a reason for whatever they turn into.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1384413#post1384413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is what I was pointing to when I said it was pointed out that it was a part of the Amalagm not the whole. This spoke of Obfuscate as a part. It has been discussed a lot in the V5 communities. What will combine with Obfuscate in the Chimerstry amalgam. Some say Dominate some say Presence. My point was though it seems you are trying to make fun of things, that comes from your misunderstanding and not where they ridiculously give Ventrue Illusions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, are you saying I'm making fun of things and that I'm misunderstanding how the amalgam powers work, or were you just using my quote to illustrate your point to Blailton? In case you were speaking very offensively to me, let me make my point clear: There has been no established text on what, if any, representation Chimerstry has in V5. Everything we're saying is speculation based on the character Shejana in the Chicago Folio, who has the Disciplines Dominate 3, Fortitude 2, Obfuscate 3, and Presence 1. As she is stated to be able to conjure illusions, we're assuming that the yet-unwritten &quot;illusion power&quot; is an amalgam of two of those Disciplines.<br /> <br /> My argument is that, based on the way that the Setites had Serpentis replaced by Protean-influenced-by-Presence, taking the standard Ravnos clan Disciplines of Animalism, Fortitude, and Chimerstry the best way to turn Chimerstry into a set of amalgam powers would be to replace it with Obfuscate and include some Obfuscate+Fortitude amalgams. Obfuscate seems like the most logical stand-in for Chimerstry in that it already reflects &quot;making people see things that aren't there&quot; via Mask of a Thousand Faces. Fortitude rather than Animalism as the amalgam makes it so that Nosferatu don't have the amalgam as an in-clan combination as well. I could see the argument being made for Dominate or Presence as the replacement instead of Obfuscate, although I don't think it fits as well and I don't think either of those Disciplines are thematic for Ravnos the way Obfuscate would be<i>. </i>And then the argument that it's some combination of Dominate+Obfuscate, Dominate+Presence, or Obfuscate+Presence based on Shejana's Disciplines then not only does that not make it unique to the Ravnos (Malkavian, Ventrue, and Setite respectively) but also removes Animalism as a Ravnos clan Discipline which I think is questionable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T11:32:19-07:00","id":1384457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1384447#post1384447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, are you saying I'm making fun of things and that I'm misunderstanding how the amalgam powers work, or were you just using my quote to illustrate your point to Blailton?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I was not saying you misunderstood. you have a clear understanding on illusions in V5 from what I am seeing. I had referred to your post as correct in that it was saying that Obfuscate was what was being talked about in proposed amalgams. <br /> <br /> Please my apologies if you thought I was speaking to you so candidly. I have no argument with your logic and understand it one of the more accurate trains of thought on the subject. though I like and feel it will be dominate or presence in the amalgam with obfuscate your logic in the use of fortitude is probable and sound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T08:16:05-07:00","id":1414919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382398-the-chicago-folio-discussion-thread?p=1384415#post1384415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that is to prevent people from turning into vampire rabbits or other ridiculous critters, Thematic means that it fits a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>HOW DARE YOU! <i>Bunnicula</i> is one of the great classics of vampire literature!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T07:39:44-07:00","id":1415068,"title":"","content":"Crossposted because I think it's okay to give these thoughts of this book:<br /> <br /> Overall, I think this is a really solid supplement that reminds me a bit of the old <i>Succubus Club</i> one for 3rd Edition. That was a collection of short adventure hooks as well as Chronicles for the player characters to experience. As such, it's kind of split between this and LET THE STREETS RUN RED but this has an excellent collection of NPCs to supplement it.<br /> <br /> I felt like the Anarch section of the book was the best part and I'm a bit biased there. However, I really enjoyed giving them the kind of attention they deserved. There's a lot of things that can change the status quo of the main game like the death of Genghis, the discovery of the List, and the decision for the Anarchs to go a lot more militant by destroying a major Kindred business. Honestly, I'm inclined to think that if the Anarchs (as is) go to war with Kevin Jackson, it'll just result in their complete destruction.<br /> <br /> Right now, Duncan MacTavish aside, they are in a seriously weakened state and at their most divided. It doesn't help that Critias is toadying to Jackson despite their 2500 year age difference. I also like the somewhat more nuanced portrayal of Kevin Jackson's rule in this book. <i>Chicago V5</i> showed that he's arguably the most powerful Prince that has ever existed in Chicago, dwarfing Lodin's control over the city due to having a weak Primogen and Helena's full support with no Menele to oppose him.<br /> <br /> This book shows that he's alienating allies like the Wolf Pack, though, and also has his subordinates refusing to obey his orders like &quot;Kill Al Capone.&quot; I actually think the fact that they didn't do it is more a sign of KJ's weakness than Al's actual threat to his regime. Al never was KJ's enemy the way he is Ballad's. It's only KJ who thought they were (probably because I can't imagine Al being the most respectful to KJ given his historical racism and treatment of rivals).<br /> <br /> The book provides a write-up for a Ravnos in 2020 and also a way to use the Sabbat in-miniature that I think are desperately needed things that make the book a &quot;must buy&quot; even though it's only a single write-up and short section. The Seven Fires are relatively unimportant in the grand scheme of things but they EXIST and give us our first real information on the state of the Black Hand outside of the Middle East.<br /> <br /> The NPCs were well-done with most of them being extremely believable and not too overpowered. While they did add a couple of Elders to the story, the majority were just a diverse collection of Neonates or Ancilla that can have a variety of interactions with the PCs. I mentioned I wish they had updated Joshua Tarponski fully but the Wolf Pack and Al Capone are enough. I think Lianna Miller, Mateo, Devin Boyce, and Zal are the standouts. Devin Boyce and the Parkie Boys, in particular replaces the Nihilists from Chicago 1st and 2nd Edition, with &quot;rowdy but kind of dumb Anarchs in need of PC help. Zal is the perfect LI for my PCs because, well, Goth girl Caitiff.<br /> <br /> The Loresheets were fine.<br /> <br /> I think the Ritual section actually was VERY needed for this game and the fact its here is kind of strange but important. It makes this book even more of a must buy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"ke